BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Competing Cultures: What Sports Tell Us About Society
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260708T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260708T210000
UID:competing-cultures-what-sports-tell-us-about-society-2026-07-08t19-00-
 00-04-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/06
 /DSC_4526-1-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scaled.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gra
 vity
DESCRIPTION:Sports are a common thread in cultural identity. So how do spo
 rts reflect\, or even transcend culture? Do they show us at our worst or b
 est?\n\nJoin award-winning executive producer and author Craig Colby as he
  explores what role sports play in society\, from shaping families to unit
 ing nations. The panel will discuss the benefits and costs of sports’ ce
 ntral role in our society.\n\nCraig will be joined by Karl Subban\, a best
 -selling author\, principal in the Toronto District School Board\, and fat
 her of three children who were signed to NHL contracts\, including P.K. Su
 bban\, Morgan Campbell\, award-winning journalist and author who writes ab
 out sports and culture\, and musician Natasha Baig\, who credits sport as 
 having shaped her discipline and sense of community long before music did.
LOCATION:Nanji Family Foundation Auditorium\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford
  Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/competing-cultures-what-sports-tell
 -us-about-society/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
